# --- App Links ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The two files that let an https invitation open the app rather than the website
# (docs/kotlin/APP-LINKS.md). Both must be reachable and both must be JSON.
#
# `apple-app-site-association` HAS NO FILE EXTENSION, which is Apple's requirement and this
# host's problem: Cloudflare infers a content type from the extension, finds none, and serves
# it as something iOS will not parse. iOS then reports nothing at all — no error, no retry,
# and universal links simply stay dead. Setting it here is the whole fix.
#
# Not cached hard, on purpose. Each is read by the OS at install and occasionally after, and
# both are expected to CHANGE without an app release: assetlinks.json gains Google's app
# signing fingerprint the day the Play listing exists. A long TTL on a file whose whole job is
# to be re-read is the same mistake the string tables above document.
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/.well-known/assetlinks.json
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate
